# Wonder Lab Studio — prototype

**Status (2026-10-07): prototype only. Nothing is deployed.** It runs on a local test server
(`127.0.0.1:8920`) and does not touch `/var/www`, nginx, systemd, the lesson-ai service or any database.

Wonder Lab Studio is the **full editor from the open-source scratch-editor 15.2.0** (`@scratch/scratch-gui`, the same
stack as `@scratch/scratch-vm` 15.2.0) embedded in a page with an **AI chat pane that drives the editor**. The student
can drag blocks by hand at any time. Every chat turn sends the student's own program and the last run back to the AI,
so the AI builds on what the student made (Kapur, productive failure). It is the planned web replacement for UCMake
(UCMake = a rebranded OpenBlock desktop app); see "Recommended path" at the end.

Screenshots: `shots/` (listed under "Screenshots"). Test results: `test/out/*.json`.

