## 1. What was built

```
 ┌──────────────── browser ───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  studio-pre.js   editor width media queries (JS + CSS) -> editor width │
 │  scratch-gui-standalone.js  (upstream, unmodified: GUI + VM + blocks + │
 │                              paint editor + renderer + audio)          │
 │      EditorState({locale:'zh-tw'}, StudioStorage)  -> vm (onVmInit)    │
 │  studio.js       boot, branding, chat pane, versions, undo             │
 │  studio-ops.js   compact program  <->  live VM blocks (one script/op)  │
 │  studio-trace.js run report (green flag / stop / keys / say / answers) │
 └──────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────▲────────┘
     POST {text, history, program, run, note, signals, studio}  │ {say, question, ops, program, focus}
 ┌──────────────▼───────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────┐
 │ server/studio_server.py  static files + STUB of /api/ai/lab           │
 │   lab_core.py (copied unchanged): sanitize_program / apply_ops /      │
 │   sanitize_run / tidy_*;  canned replies, or WL_REAL=1 -> lab_turn()  │
 └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

| Requirement | How |
|---|---|
| Full editor, left | `@scratch/scratch-gui` **15.2.0 standalone build** (`dist/scratch-gui-standalone.js`, exports `EditorState` + `createStandaloneRoot`). Palette, workspace, stage, sprite list, costumes and sounds tabs, paint editor, sound editor, debug-strategies modal, File menu all work. Locale `zh-tw`. No build step and no fork: the library is consumed as published. |
| Chat pane, right | `src/index.html` + `studio.css`. Side by side from 1280 px wide (pane 360 px). Below 1280 px (iPad landscape 1024) the pane is a drawer opened by the 「AI 學伴」 button in the menu bar. `studio-pre.js` rewrites the editor's viewport media queries (JS `matchMedia` and the CSS `@media` rules) so the editor lays itself out for the width it really has (at 1440 it uses its own "constrained stage" layout, as on a 1024 screen). |
| Student drags blocks | Untouched editor behaviour. |
| AI drives the editor | `vm` from the GUI's `onVmInit` prop. The reply is the **same shape lab_core emits**: `ops` = `apply_ops()` output (`{do:"set_script"|"delete_script", sprite, id, n}`), blocks taken from the reply's merged `program`. `studio-ops.js` is a port of `wonderlab.js` `compile()`, but writes **one script at a time** into the live VM (`target.blocks.createBlock`), then `vm.emitWorkspaceUpdate()` so the GUI redraws. A replaced script keeps its position; a new one goes into a free spot in the visible workspace. Changed scripts get a teal outline for 8 s and are scrolled into view. Same whitelist (`src/opcodes.json` = `wonderlab-src/src/opcodes.json` = `lab_opcodes.json`), pen extension loaded on demand. |
| Student work flows back | Each turn sends `program` = a **decompile of the live VM** into the compact model (hand-built scripts get ids `h1, h2…`; AI scripts keep their id through the block id `wl_<id>_…`, which also survives .sb3 save/load), `run` = the trace report (ported from `wonderlab.js` run/sample/report; starts on the green flag or a clicked script, ends on stop), `signals` `{runs, stops, undo}`, `note` after 上一步, and a prototype extension `studio`: live sprite/costume/backdrop names, the editing sprite, `hand_edits` (scripts added/changed/removed by hand since the last AI turn) and `unsupported` (scripts that use blocks outside the whitelist; those blocks are never sent as blocks). |
| Versions | Every settled hand edit (1.2 s after the last change), every AI turn, load and restore is a version: time, source (開始 / 自己改 / AI 改 / AI 回覆 / 載入 / 還原), compact program, unsupported list, block count, the student's words / AI's `say`, the **run report of that version**, and the full project JSON (`vm.toJSON()`; assets are cached so painted costumes restore). Tab 「版本」 lists them with 「還原這個版本」 and 「匯出全部版本（JSON）」 for a later consolidation step (compare failed attempts with the working one). 「上一步」 restores the version before the last AI change and tells the AI (same note as lab.js). Kept in memory and in `localStorage` (last 60; project JSON for the last 15). |
| .sb3 | The editor's own 檔案 > 下載到你的電腦 / 從你的電腦載入. Round trip verified (UI and `vm.saveProjectSb3()`). |
| Stub endpoint | `server/studio_server.py` on 8920 (`POST /api/ai/lab/<anything>`). Canned, keyword-based replies that **build on the student's own green-flag script** (e.g. 「一直走」 adds 重複無限次 + 移動 10 點 to it); any other message gets an observe reply that describes the student's program and last run. Replies go through the real `lab_core` validators, so they are exactly what the service would accept. |
| Branding / licence | See sections 3 and 4. Licence + source page `/NOTICE.html`, AGPL source download `/source.tar.gz`. |

