Stop the server with Ctrl+C. Ports: 8920 (stub) and 8921 (real-model test) only.

### Pointing it at the real `/api/ai/lab` endpoint

1. Front-end: set the endpoint before `studio.js` loads, e.g.
   `<script>window.WL_API = '/api/ai/lab/files/L4/lessons/<slug>';</script>` and serve the page from the same origin as
   lesson-ai (requests use `credentials: 'same-origin'`, so the portal login cookie is sent). The client already
   handles `{ok:false, reason}`, 429/413/502 the way `lab.js` does (message + keeps the student's words).
2. lab_core needs a **studio mode** (not done, nothing in ycltesthk-portals was edited):
   - `Ctx` / `sanitize_program` / `apply_ops` validate sprite names against the lesson's fixed sprites. In the Studio
     the student adds, renames and paints sprites, so the lesson context must be built from `body.studio.targets`
     (sanitised: names ≤ 40 chars, word filter, caps on counts), as `lesson_from()` in `server/studio_server.py` does.
   - a free-creation brief (goal / question path) for lessons that open the Studio, or the lesson's own brief;
   - two prompt lines: 【學生自己改過】 from `studio.hand_edits` and 【AI 看不懂的積木】 from `studio.unsupported`;
   - storage: `lab_programs` keeps the compact program only; the Studio needs the .sb3 (assets) and the version list
     per student, server side.
   - `MAX_BODY` (64 000) is enough for the snapshot; `studio` adds about 0.5–2 KB.
3. Verified with the copied `lab_core.lab_turn` and DeepSeek (`deepseek-chat`), 2 calls, `test/out/real_turns.json`:
   the student drags 「當綠旗被點擊 + 移動 10 點」, runs it, says 「我想佢一直行」 → the model **rewrote the student's own
   script `h1`** into 「當綠旗被點擊 → 重複無限次 { 移動 10 點 }」 (applied in the live editor, same position), asked for a
   prediction; then 「佢行出咗舞台」 → `observe`, no ops, one question (PF rules held). Screenshot `shots/10-…`.

