## 5. What works (verified)

`python3 test/e2e.py` — **25/25 checks pass** (`test/out/results.json`), Chrome 153 headless:

- editor ready with the neutral default sprite; zh-tw UI, block text and paint editor;
- hand-dragged 「當綠旗被點擊 + 移動 10 點」 appears in the snapshot; the green flag run is traced (start [0,0] → end [10,0]);
- 1st AI turn: request carries the hand-built program, the run report and `hand_edits`; the reply's ops land in the
  live workspace, extending the student's own script (4 blocks, outlined);
- the student drags 「右轉 15 度」 into the AI's loop → captured; 2nd turn sends it, and the AI's next change keeps it;
- version history start → hand → hand → AI → hand → AI; the run report is stored with the version that ran;
- 上一步 restores the program before the last AI turn and the next request carries the 上一步 note + `undo: 1`;
- a block outside the whitelist (停播所有音效) is reported in `unsupported`, never sent; the AI's change to that script is
  placed **next to it** and the student's script is left as it was (with a chat notice);
- .sb3: 檔案 > 下載到你的電腦 → new page → 從你的電腦載入 → same program (and `vm.saveProjectSb3 → loadProject`);
- costumes tab (paint editor), sounds tab and 除錯方式 modal open; no "Scratch" text or link anywhere visible;
- iPad width 1024x768 (Chromium, touch, iPad UA): no horizontal scroll, drawer opens, AI turn applies blocks;
- no console errors; no request outside the local server.

Also: File > 新建專案 loads the neutral default; the paint button creates 「角色2」 and opens the paint editor;
**WebKit** (Playwright WebKit, iPad gen 7 profile at 1024x768): loads in 2.7 s locally, no errors, AI turn applies
3 blocks, green flag runs (sprite to x = 267), run report correct, no horizontal scroll (`shots/11`, `shots/12`).

## 6. What does not work / limits

- **No asset libraries, no surprise sprite, no extension library** (hidden, see section 4). Only pen; music, video
  sensing, text-to-speech, translate and all hardware extensions are unavailable. Painting, uploading images/sounds and
  recording work.
- **Branding is patched at run time** on an unmodified bundle: DOM edits keyed on aria-labels / class fragments
  (`main-button`, `tutorials-button`), a locale-message override, `builtinHelper._store` for the default project.
  Each scratch-gui upgrade can break them silently. Language switching is off (only zh-tw and en were patched).
- **Workspace access goes through React internals** (fiber walk to the Blocks container for `workspace`). Only used for
  placing new scripts in view, the outline and scrolling; if it breaks, ops still apply (fallback placement).
- After an AI turn the workspace's own undo (Ctrl+Z) history is cleared (the GUI reloads the workspace). 上一步 and
  版本 cover it.
- If the student edits a script **while** a turn is in flight and the AI replaces that script, the edit is overwritten
  (it is still in 版本 if it had settled for 1.2 s). The real service needs a "program changed since sent" check.
- Hand-made script ids (`h1`, `h2` …) are renumbered by order after an .sb3 reload; AI script ids survive.
- Versions live only in this browser (memory + localStorage; on a shared device they persist until cleared). Painted
  costumes of older versions restore only in the same session. No server-side history yet.
- The stub is keyword-based; only 2 real model turns were run. No lab_core change was made, so the real endpoint
  cannot be used yet (section 3).
- iPad: tested in headless Chromium with an iPad UA and in Playwright WebKit — **not on a real iPad**; touch dragging of
  blocks was not tested (only taps). Below 1280 px the chat is a drawer that covers the stage while open.
- Upstream console **warnings** remain (no errors): Blockly 12 deprecations (`getVariablesOfType`), "pen_* overwrites
  previous definition" (pen re-registered on each project load), `FieldColourSlider` DOM init, `flyoutinflater`,
  Canvas2D `willReadFrequently`. The copied lab_core prints "tagging disabled" (no taxonomy file; harmless).
- Install size: `node_modules` 1.1 GB (scratch-gui's full dependency tree); the served `dist/` is 120 MB without
  source maps (68 MB tutorial/extension images, 14 MB MediaPipe), of which a cold load fetches 5.8 MB.

